{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"The test harness will keep C and Rust object graphs separate, since opaque pointers cannot cross libraries. Comparisons will snapshot return codes, output buffers, offsets, selector values, and serialized bytes from each side; function addresses and allocated pointer values are deliberately not compared."}}
